WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:08.780
The United States has recognized
Juan Guaidó as the legitimate president

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:13.500
of Venezuela, launching an international
campaign to oust the narcodictator

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:18.270
Nicolas Maduro. More than 50 governments
have backed Guaidó as Venezuela's

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:22.830
constitutional president. Guaidó has
called on Maduro to cede power to a

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:26.220
transitional government and he has
attempted to win the Venezuelan military

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:30.390
to his cause. Thus far,
Maduro and his criminal cronies

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:34.290
have resisted US sanctions and
diplomatic pressure. They have amassed

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:39.120
fortunes from stolen oil revenue in
cocaine trafficking, so they have simply

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:43.040
too much to lose. US diplomats
have called on military leaders

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:47.820
to oust Maduro as well. However,
an April rebellion plotted by Guaidó's team

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:52.160
failed after producing only a
handful of defectors. Guaidó has now

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:56.860
agreed to negotiations, but Maduro may
only offer elections where the regime

00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:01.360
holds all the cards. Many predict that
Maduro will never step aside for Guaidó,

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:06.500
unless he is forced out by Venezuelan
patriots fighting for their country.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:09.330
Do you think the current US
strategy will produce a change in

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:13.710
Venezuela? Let us know in our poll, and
let us know what other topics you'd like

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:18.570
our scholars to cover in 60 seconds, and
be sure to LIKE and subscribe for more

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:22.280
research and videos from AEI.

